  "text": "I was angry too. I remember one time, my mom said I should not be friends with someone because they were not good enough. I was 16 at that time. I felt so angry and hurt. I told her that I could choose my own friends and that I didn't need her approval. I said that I was old enough to make my own decisions and that I would not let her dictate who I could and couldn't be friends with. I remember feeling so scared and worried that she would be angry with me, but I also felt a sense of relief and empowerment. I realized that I had the right to choose my own friends and that I didn't have to let her control my life.\n\nIt's okay to feel angry and hurt when someone tries to control you. It's normal to feel that way. But it's also important to remember that you have the right to make your own decisions and to choose your own path in life. You don't have to let anyone else dictate what you can and can't do.\n\nIt sounds like you're feeling really angry and hurt right now, and that's okay. It's okay to feel those emotions. But also remember that you are strong and capable, and you can make your own decisions. You don't have to let your mom's opinions control you.\n\nHow does that sound? Does that make sense to you?",
